      "area": "contact",
      "claim": "A parent reports that strangers can message or voice chat with your child in Google Classroom.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "Kids can interact with other students and even teachers by text and video using Hangouts or the chat function in Meet."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D520]",
      "area": "money",
      "claim": "The platform does not push in-app purchases, loot boxes, pay-to-win or subscription traps.",
      "stance": "neutral",
      "quote": "Google Classroom is a class-organization platform that incorporates Google's core products (Google Docs, Sheets, Slides, Drive, etc.) so students can access everything they need for a class, including homework assignments, group projects, files, and even Google Hangouts to chat with the teacher or the entire class."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D520]",
      "area": "data",
      "claim": "Google may collect student data from some Classroom tools, such as YouTube, if they're enabled.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "Classroom allows students to see what's due, complete assignments, post messages, and more in virtual classes set up by their teachers. The fact that it's paperless and offers built-in opportunities for kids to practice responsible digital skills are great bonuses. ... Google can collect student data from some of the Classroom tools, such as YouTube, if they're enabled."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D520]",
      "area": "age_gating",
      "claim": "A parent reports that the age gate does not work in practice; children can bypass it.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "Google pitches the platform to teachers as \"mission control for your classroom\" -- and it definitely streamlines homework, remote learning, and organization. But as more schools move toward using Google Classroom, it's a good idea to familiarize yourself with its capabilities so you can best support your kid's online learning."
    },
